---
description: QFile/resource load helpers must not collapse open, read, and empty-file failures into an empty QString
globs: **/*.{h,hpp,cpp}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Load failures are not empty content

Returning `{}` from `QFile::open` makes missing resources, permission errors, short reads, and empty files look the same. Callers then log a generic “Failed to load” with only the path (`Style::ApplyLightTheme`).

Return a small result (`content` + `errorMessage`), or `optional` plus out-error. Record `errorString()` on open **and** after `readAll()` (`QFileDevice::error()`). Treat successful open of empty bytes as `"file is empty"`, not as success.

Empty `content` with empty `errorMessage` is success only when empty is a valid payload. Theme QSS is not.

```cpp
// BAD — open failure, read error, and empty file are all ""
if (!file.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly | QIODevice::Text)) return {};
return QString::fromUtf8(file.readAll());

// GOOD
if (!file.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly | QIODevice::Text)) {
  result.errorMessage = file.errorString();
  return result;
}
const QByteArray bytes = file.readAll();
if (file.error() != QFileDevice::NoError) {
  result.errorMessage = file.errorString();
  return result;
}
```
